// The turbo_ui package is a reusable immediate-mode cell UI layered over
// core/tui. It owns no terminal, renderer, event loop, application document,
// or compiler state. A caller begins one frame with a borrowed Surface and one
// already-decoded event, invokes ordinary widget procedures in deterministic
// draw order, and ends the frame before either borrow expires.
//
// State retains only interaction identity across frames: hot/active/focused
// IDs, the active/modal window, one popup, and direct-manipulation metadata.
// Persistent values such as text storage, menu/combobox selection, checkbox
// contents, window bounds, visibility, and z-order remain in explicit
// caller-owned records. This keeps the library independently reusable by the
// gallery, editor, and later applications without callbacks, inheritance, a
// retained widget tree, or hidden allocation.
//
// The package depends only on core/tui for cells and core/unicode for clipped
// grapheme painting. It performs no I/O. Relevant Draft specification: sections
// 5-7; core/tui owns the Unicode cell and rendering contract.
package turbo_ui

// Widget_Id is the explicit cross-frame identity supplied by the application.
// Zero is reserved for "no widget/window" so a zero State is ready for its
// first frame. IDs need only be unique among live controls in one application.
pub Widget_Id :: u64

pub No_Widget :: cast[Widget_Id](0)
